Article 1: Scope of Deposit Certificate Dispute Cases
(1) Dispute cases filed with the People's Court by a deposit certificate holder using the deposit certificate as important evidence;
(2) Dispute cases filed with the People's Court by a party using vouchers such as credit slips, statements of account, and deposit contracts as primary evidence;
(3) Dispute cases filed by a financial institution with the People's Court requesting confirmation that vouchers such as deposit certificates, credit slips, statements of account, and deposit contracts are invalid;
(4) Loan dispute cases in the form of deposit certificates.
